.TH TATAMI.CONF 5 "" "tatami"
.SH NAME
tatami.conf \- configuration of tatami and tatamk, repository lists and hooks
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tatami.conf
configures
.BR tatami (8)
and
.BR tatamk (8).
It is optional: if it is missing, empty or unreadable the built\-in defaults are used
and tatami works offline with the local repository
.BR /var/lib/tatami/packages .
A file given with
.B \-\-config
must exist.
.PP
All paths in this manual are relative to the installation root
.RB ( \-\-root ,
default
.BR / ).
They are the defaults of the build; the base directories
.RB ( /etc ,
.B /var/lib/tatami
and
.BR /var/cache/tatami )
can be changed when tatami is compiled.
.SH SYNTAX
The file has one entry per line.
Empty lines and lines starting with
.B #
are ignored.
.PP
A setting is
.IB NAME " = " value
with optional blanks around the equals sign; the value may be quoted.
A line that is not a setting is a rule (see below).
An unknown setting or a malformed line is an error that names the file and the line.
.SH SETTINGS
.TP
.B PKG_EXT
A fixed package extension without the leading dot, for example
.BR tar.pkg .
By default packages are named
.B \&.tar.\fIcompression\fR
and every compression is accepted.
.TP
.B PKG_COMPRESSION
.BR tatamk 's
compression: one of
.BR gz ,
.B zst
(the default),
.BR xz ,
.BR bz2 ,
.BR lz4 ,
.B lzma
or
.BR none .
.TP
.B ARCH
Architecture of the target system; the default is
.BR "uname \-m" .
Packages of any other architecture are refused;
.B noarch
packages always fit.
A colon\-separated list, such as
.BR x86_64:i686 ,
allows more (multilib).
.BR tatamk
builds for the first entry.
.TP
.B REPO_DIRS
Repositories as paths or URLs separated by blanks, used when no
.B repos.conf
exists (see
.BR REPOSITORIES ).
.TP
.B FETCHCMD
The command that downloads a remote file.
.B %URL%
and
.B %DEST%
are replaced; both must appear.
It is run directly, not through a shell, so quoting protects blanks but nothing in a
URL is interpreted.
tatami reads the command's standard error for percentages such as the ones
.B curl \-#
prints and shows its own progress bar instead.
Default:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fBcurl \-f \-L \-# "%URL%" \-o "%DEST%"\fR
.fi
.RE
.IP
It is never used for local paths or
.B file://
repositories.
.TP
.B PUBKEY
The Ed25519 public key (64 hexadecimal digits, or base64 of the 32 bytes) that signs
the remote repositories, as printed by
.BR "tatami keygen" .
For every remote
.B repo.solv
and package a
.B .sig
file is fetched and verified; a failure aborts.
Local paths and
.B file://
repositories are trusted and never checked.
Without a
.B PUBKEY
remote repositories are refused;
.B PUBKEY = none
accepts unsigned remote data (the SHA\-256 checksums of the index are still checked).
.TP
.B HoldPkg
Space\-separated names of installed packages that are never upgraded or removed as a
side effect by a transaction.
They are handed to the solver as locked, and
.B tatami upgrade
prints
.B Skipping upgrade for held package: \fIname\fB (\fIold\fB \-> \fInew\fB)
for each one that has a newer version.
The setting may be repeated and the names add up.
A package named in the
.B install
or
.B remove
command itself is not held for that command:
an explicit request wins.
.TP
.B BULKHEAD
.B yes
(the default) or
.BR no :
whether
.BR tatamk
builds in a
.BR bwrap (1)
sandbox.
.SH RULES
.IB EVENT " " pattern " " ACTION
.PP
.I EVENT
is
.B UPGRADE
or
.BR INSTALL ,
.I pattern
a POSIX extended regular expression matched against the path of a package file
relative to the root, without a leading slash (for example
.BR ^etc/.*$ ),
and
.I ACTION
is
.B YES
or
.BR NO .
For each file the last matching rule wins; a file that no rule matches is treated as
.BR YES .
.TP
.B UPGRADE ... NO
Marks a configuration file.
When an upgrade brings a different version of a file that exists,
the new version is installed and the existing file is renamed to
.IB file .old
(an identical file is left alone, an earlier
.B .old
is replaced).
A rollback puts the original back.
.TP
.B INSTALL ... NO
The file is not installed at all.
.PP
The default configuration has one rule:
.PP
.RS
.B UPGRADE ^etc/.*$ NO
.RE
.SH REPOSITORIES
Repositories are listed in
.B /etc/tatami/repos.conf
and in the files
.B /etc/tatami/repos.d/*.conf
(read in alphabetical order), one per line:
.PP
.RS
.nf
.IB name " = " url
.fi
.RE
.PP
.I name
is made of letters, digits,
.BR . ,
.B _
and
.BR \- ;
it must be unique.
.I url
is one of
.TP
.B /path or file:///path
A local directory of packages, read in place.
If it contains a
.B repo.solv
(written by
.BR "tatami index" )
that index is used, otherwise the packages are scanned.
.TP
.B http://, https://, ftp://
A remote repository.
.B tatami update
downloads its
.B repo.solv
to
.BR /var/lib/tatami/repos/\fIname\fB/ ,
and
.B tatami install
downloads packages to
.BR /var/cache/tatami/packages ,
both with
.BR FETCHCMD ,
and verifies them (see
.BR PUBKEY ).
Publish such a repository by putting the packages and the files made by
.BR tatamk (8)
(the index and the signatures) on a server.
.PP
If the list is empty or the files do not exist, the
.B REPO_DIRS
setting is used, and failing that the local directory
.BR /var/lib/tatami/packages .
Nothing is ever downloaded unless a remote repository is configured explicitly.
When a version is in several repositories, the one listed first wins.
.SH HOOKS
Hook files
.B /etc/tatami/hooks.d/\fIname\fB.hook
say what to run after a transaction.
They have
.I Key = value
lines:
.TP
.B Trigger
A POSIX extended regular expression, matched against the paths the transaction added,
changed or removed (relative to the root; directories end in
.BR / ).
May be repeated; the hook runs if any matches.
.TP
.B Operation
Optional: any of
.BR install ,
.B upgrade
and
.BR remove .
The default is all.
.TP
.B Needs
Optional: a path that must exist in the root for the hook to run.
.TP
.B Exec
The command.
Blanks separate the words, quotes group them, and there is no shell.
.B %ROOT%
is replaced by the installation root, and
.B TATAMI_ROOT
is set.
.PP
A hook runs at most once per transaction, after the commit.
A failing hook is reported but does not undo the transaction; a malformed one is
detected before anything is changed.
The installed example runs
.B ldconfig \-r %ROOT%
when libraries change.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/tatami/tatami.conf
This file.
.TP
.B /etc/tatami/repos.conf, /etc/tatami/repos.d/*.conf
Repository lists.
.TP
.B /etc/tatami/hooks.d/*.hook
Hooks.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
PUBKEY      = 05ad836299e2a530bbffd0b4da78f6bc88189250b32c654c4ef8db13ea09e3be
HoldPkg     = linux glibc
ARCH        = x86_64
PKG_COMPRESSION = zst

UPGRADE     ^etc/.*$     NO
.fi
.PP
and in
.BR /etc/tatami/repos.conf :
.PP
.nf
core  = https://packages.example.org/core
local = /srv/packages
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tatami (8),
.BR tatamk (8)
